# $project_name

Built with [Aegra](https://github.com/aegra/aegra) -- a self-hosted LangSmith Deployments alternative.

## Setup

```bash
cp .env.example .env       # Configure your environment
uv sync                    # Install dependencies
uv run aegra dev           # Start developing!
```

## Model Configuration

Set `Context.model` in `src/$slug/context.py` using `provider/model`, for example
`openai/gpt-4o-mini`. Only the first slash separates the provider from the model ID;
`openai/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3` uses provider `openai` and model ID
`deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3`.

For an OpenAI-compatible gateway, set `OPENAI_BASE_URL` to its API endpoint and
`OPENAI_API_KEY` to its API key in `.env`. The provider and model must both be
nonempty; values such as `openai/`, `/gpt-4o`, and `gpt-4o` are rejected.

## Project Structure

```
$slug/
|-- aegra.json            # Graph configuration
|-- pyproject.toml        # Project dependencies
|-- .env.example          # Environment variable template
|-- src/$slug/
|   |-- __init__.py
|   |-- graph.py          # Your agent graph
|   |-- state.py          # Input and internal state
|   |-- prompts.py        # System prompt templates
|   |-- context.py        # Runtime configuration
|   +-- utils.py          # Utility functions
|-- docker-compose.yml    # Docker Compose (PostgreSQL + API)
+-- Dockerfile
```
